    "context_text": "# R5 complete current-helper provenance request, delivered in bounded chunks\n\nThis is the authorized narrow Phase 4 provenance refresh for Fablebook v0.4 Phase 3 Plan 03-05. The owner authorized scoped refresh (INT-20261118-03).\n\n## Exact source and prior request state\n\nAnalyze only the complete current helper `test/support/guard_aggregate_reconciliation_evidence.ex`: 2,182 lines, 79,280 bytes, SHA-256 `5aeb1631123bfaf1a6914c3e324486adef3369b762bbdc0a57a7f93d2d16e1f1`. Its full-file identity is fixed in this schedule. R1 is consumed-incomplete; R2 and R3 are consumed-verified against prior helper SHA-256 `75d23e5b48d17c632fd42c3d052aea7b1f25531ca359d897fc40ae577f61bbd6`; R4 is consumed-incomplete because a wrapper truncated its middle. Never replay R1/R2/R3/R4 or use R4's partial output as evidence. R5 is the one fresh request for the complete current file.\n\n## Analysis purpose\n\nFrom this exact helper only, identify full function spans relevant to the saved coverage flag, source selectors and association/gap collectors, caller crosswalk, and nested digest/canonicalization. Compare the current helper identity to the historical generator identity. Where historical generation is not proven, retain `generator_revision_mismatch` and keep the historical claim unresolved. Do not infer semantics from a saved flag or count.\n\n## Chunked one-use delivery\n\nThe complete file is split into six ordered, contiguous chunks. Each scheduled chunk binds its exact byte and line range, byte count and SHA-256 and is at most 14,000 bytes. Receive each chunk in its own bounded tool result, checking its completion marker and hash. Do not analyze any partial result. Concatenate all six exact byte spans and require the complete-file length and SHA-256 above before source analysis. The six results together are one R5 emission; do not request or read any chunk twice. If any chunk is incomplete, mark R5 consumed-incomplete and stop without retry.\n\n## Boundaries and retained stops\n\nNo other source or test body is in scope. Do not inspect OTP/library target bodies or external callers, invoke audited code or callbacks, evaluate runtime input, deserialize untrusted terms, generate code, install dependencies, or modify application source. Keep source resolution unresolved, caller closure incomplete, legacy digest unresolved unless exact safely established, candidate null, implementation unauthorized, aggregate gate open, actual-library collision unknown, Macro caller-AST/explanation checkpoints unresolved, Walking Skeleton blocked, SEC-01 Pending, and all existing security stops.\n\n## Count contract\n\nThe direct count input is this exact UTF-8 context, two LF, `# Exact scheduled source selection`, one LF, and the entire scheduled source file. Count only via `POST https://api.openai.com/v1/responses/input_tokens` for `gpt-6-luna`, with generation false. The configured 200,000-token limit is per-request context fit only; no cumulative assistant-output ceiling or reserve blocks execution. After metadata-only review, fresh Phase 4 execute preflight, direct count, and one-use gate pass, deliver the six scheduled chunks once.\n\n## Evidence inputs\n\nCurrent Phase 3/4 plans and replans, intent, current metadata/provenance artifacts, active resource ledger, and immutable R1/R2/R3/R4 receipts are separately hash-bound in this schedule. Use no unbound artifact to make a claim.\n",
